From 93167a7d557af015d6e7c8bb8a72110e53b0e8af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:43:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the BT.2390 curve with the knee of ITU-R BT.2390

The BT.2390 curve of the bridge (the tone mapping method "Reference
(BT.2390)" to an SDR output, the "BT.2390 (ITU-R)" curve of a mapping to
an HDR10 display, Dolby Vision Low-Latency) took libplacebo's default
knee offset, 1.0: KS = 2 maxLum - 1. The EETF of ITU-R BT.2390 puts the
knee at KS = 1.5 maxLum - 0.5 (Report ITU-R BT.2408-9 Annex 5, step 2,
the text that Report BT.2390-12 now refers to for display mapping), an
offset of 0.5; libplacebo's header says that its default differs from
the spec. Below the knee the picture goes out as mastered, and the
default knee compressed much of what the display can show: a master of
1000 cd/m2 on an SDR output with its white at 203 cd/m2 was compressed
from 36 cd/m2 up instead of from 88, and one of 4000 cd/m2 from 5.8 up
instead of from 40.

The offset is set to 0.5 where the curve is BT.2390, in
display_mapping(), which the mapping and the gamut mapping table made
ahead both take.

Measured on the software bridge (Mesa llvmpipe), a neutral ramp of
every 10-bit code of a plain PQ picture, masters of 1000, 4000 and
10000 cd/m2 mapped to SDR whites of 100 and 203 (gamma 2.4) and 300
(gamma 2.2) and to HDR10 displays of 600 and 1400 cd/m2, against the
EETF computed from the text of the report: within 0.17 of a code
(10-bit SDR, 12-bit PQ) in all 15 cases; before, 24 to 153 codes away
from it in the 14 that map (a display of 1400 cd/m2 holds a master of
1000: nothing is mapped, the same picture). A master of 1000 cd/m2 at
an SDR white of 203: 100 cd/m2 of it now go out at 99.3, not 86.7.

Real pictures, profile 7 FEL with the enhancement layer, 8 of each of
two films, the trim pass of the metadata on, mapped to SDR at 203
cd/m2: where the display can show the source, Delta E ITP (ITU-R
BT.2124) against it 0.82 on average instead of 3.12 (95th percentile
6.3 instead of 17.4), the mean light 70.6 cd/m2 instead of 65.1 (80.0
in the source). What is brighter than the display's white keeps less
of its gradation (the spread of its intensity 35 % of the source's
instead of 44 %): that is the trade libplacebo's default makes. On
displays of 600 cd/m2 and more these films (scene peaks up to 1127
cd/m2) hardly move: fewer than 0.05 % of their pixels by more than 1
Delta E, at most 5.2 on a display of 600, 0.9 on one of 1000, nothing
on one of 1387.

Nothing else moves: the spline does not read the offset (its pictures
the same bytes in all 15 cases), nor does pl_tone_map_st2094_40, which
takes the place of this curve for HDR10+ metadata that carry their own
curve; the gamut mapping table does not depend on it
(pl_color_map_gamut_table() keys it by the gamut mapping alone), and
the one made ahead is still the one each mapping takes (60 of 60
renders).
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h |  5 +++++
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c  | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h
index bb06b6c..19e6e5b 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_placebo.h
@@ -60,6 +60,11 @@ enum dvbridge_hdr10_curve {
     DVBRIDGE_HDR10_CURVE_SPLINE = 0, /* libplacebo's default tone mapping */
     DVBRIDGE_HDR10_CURVE_BT2390 = 1, /* the EETF of ITU-R BT.2390 */
 };
+/* Hades: the knee of the BT.2390 curve, where the EETF of ITU-R BT.2390 puts it: KS = 1.5 maxLum - 0.5 (Report
+ * ITU-R BT.2408-9 (03/2026) Annex 5, step 2, the text that BT.2390-12 now refers to for display mapping). It is the
+ * knee offset of libplacebo's pl_tone_map_bt2390, whose KS is (1 + offset) maxLum - offset; libplacebo's own
+ * default offset is 1.0 (KS = 2 maxLum - 1), which its header says differs from the spec. */
+#define DVBRIDGE_BT2390_KNEE_OFFSET 0.5f
 #define DVBRIDGE_HDR10_PEAK_MIN 10.0f
 #define DVBRIDGE_HDR10_PEAK_MAX 10000.0f
 /* Hades: the signal the mapped picture is written in. HDR10 (the default, 0): PQ in BT.2020, for a
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index 63aec86..c90f03e 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -2120,6 +2120,17 @@ static void display_mapping(const struct dvbridge_hdr10_mapping *m, const int *s
     *params = pl_color_map_default_params;
     params->tone_mapping_function =
         m->curve == DVBRIDGE_HDR10_CURVE_BT2390 ? &pl_tone_map_bt2390 : &pl_tone_map_spline;
+    /* Hades: the BT.2390 curve with the knee of the EETF of ITU-R BT.2390, KS = 1.5 maxLum - 0.5
+     * (DVBRIDGE_BT2390_KNEE_OFFSET): up to that knee the picture goes out as mastered, and only what is above it
+     * is compressed. With libplacebo's default offset of 1.0 (KS = 2 maxLum - 1) the roll-off began far lower:
+     * a master of 1000 cd/m2 shown on an SDR output with its white at 203 cd/m2 was compressed from 36 cd/m2 up
+     * instead of from 88, its 100 cd/m2 came out at 86.7 instead of 99.3, and one of 4000 cd/m2 was compressed
+     * from 5.8 cd/m2 up instead of from 40. The spline does not read the offset, nor does the curve of an HDR10+
+     * picture's own metadata, which takes the place of this one (map_hdr10plus()); the gamut mapping table does
+     * not depend on it (pl_color_map_gamut_table() keys the table by the gamut mapping alone), so the one made
+     * ahead (gamut_ahead_start(), the same parameters) is still the one the mapping asks for. */
+    if (m->curve == DVBRIDGE_HDR10_CURVE_BT2390)
+        params->tone_constants.knee_offset = DVBRIDGE_BT2390_KNEE_OFFSET;
     params->gamut_mapping = &pl_gamut_map_perceptual;
     params->metadata = PL_HDR_METADATA_ANY;
     params->inverse_tone_mapping = false;
-- 
2.53.0

